## Conventional Commits

This project follows [Conventional Commits](https://www.conventionalcommits.org/en/v1.0.0/).
Every commit message starts with one of:

* `feat` — new user-visible capability
* `fix` — bug fix
* `docs` — documentation only
* `refactor` — code change without behavior or feature change
* `test` — adding or fixing tests
* `chore` — build, deps, tooling
* `ci` — CI configuration
* `perf` — performance improvement
* `style` — formatting, no behavior change
* `revert` — reverts a previous commit

Optional scope in parens (`feat(timer): …`). Breaking changes get `!` and a
`BREAKING CHANGE:` footer (`feat!: drop legacy v1 API`).

The pre-commit `commit-msg` hook (see [`.pre-commit-config.yaml`](./.pre-commit-config.yaml))
blocks non-conformant messages locally; CI re-checks on the merge commit.

